######## STEPS 1-2 RESULT (38386, BACKUP port1.0.1) — PASS ########
access-list hardware acl-qos-b : permit ip 10.10.10.1/32 any
class-map  cm-qos-b            : match access-group acl-qos-b
policy-map pm-qos-b / class cm-qos-b : set cos 3   (deliberately different from the
                                       master's 5 so the two results cannot be confused)
interface port1.0.1            : service-policy input pm-qos-b
  show policy-map pm-qos-b -> Interfaces: port1.0.1 ; Set CoS: 3

Sent 20 tagged frames (prio 0) eth3 -> port1.0.1 (BACKUP), captured on eth2:
     10  src=10.10.10.1  prio=3     <- MATCHES policy, CoS CHANGED 0 -> 3
     10  src=10.10.10.2  prio=0     <- does NOT match, CoS UNCHANGED
=> STEPS 1-2 PASS on the BACKUP member, identical behaviour to the MASTER (38388).
   Policies are ingress-only and independent: the master's policy on port2.0.1 had no
   effect on traffic ingressing port1.0.1.

