######## ⚠️ MEASUREMENT ARTEFACT (see 38388.log for the full diagnosis) ########
Throughput measured via rx_bytes reads 0.00 Mbps unless frames are addressed to the
receiving NIC's real MAC - the NIC hardware-filters everything else, and it looks
exactly like total packet loss. Proven not to be the DUT by re-running with NO policy
applied (still 0.00) and by the switch's own egress counters showing it forwarding
30,013 packets. Pcaps were rebuilt with the real NIC MACs before any result below.

######## STEPS 3-4 RESULT (38386, BACKUP port1.0.1) — PASS ########
policy-map pm-qos-b / class cm-qos-b:
    police single-rate 20000 20000 40000 action drop-red
    police counters
  A DIFFERENT CIR (20 Mbps) from the master's (10 Mbps) was used deliberately, so the
  result demonstrates the policer honours the CONFIGURED value rather than converging
  on some fixed behaviour.

  CONTROL, no policy : offered 49.99 Mbps -> received 48.68 Mbps
  WITH 20 Mbps policer: offered 49.99 Mbps -> received 19.60 Mbps  (CIR = 20.00 Mbps)
=> Ingress traffic limited to the configured rate, within ~2% of CIR. STEPS 3-4 PASS.

######## VERDICT 38386 (BACKUP): PASS — all four steps ########
Identical behaviour to the MASTER (38388). QoS marking and policing show no
master/backup difference; policies are ingress-only and independent per port.
